problemStatement:
## Improve the Card Contrast

You are given the following HTML and CSS for a product card. It fails WCAG AA contrast checks. Identify the issues and fix them **only** by modifying the CSS. You may not change the HTML.

```html
<div class="card">
  <h3 class="card-title">Wireless Headphones</h3>
  <p class="card-price">$49.99</p>
  <p class="card-desc">High‑quality sound, noise cancelling.</p>
  <button class="card-btn">Add to Cart</button>
</div>
```
```css
.card {
  background: #f0f0f0; /* light grey */
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
}
.card-title {
  color: #999; /* light grey */
  font-size: 18px;
}
.card-price {
  color: #0a0; /* green */
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
}
.card-desc {
  color: #bbb;
}
.card-btn {
  background: #0a0;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  padding: 10px;
}
```

Run the hex codes through a contrast checker and adjust colours to meet AA (normal text 4.5:1, large text 3:1, UI component contrast 3:1). Keep the design visually similar.

solutionCode:
.card {
  background: #ffffff;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #949494; /* 3:1 against white */
}
.card-title {
  color: #595959; /* 4.5:1 against white */
  font-size: 18px;
}
.card-price {
  color: #007a00; /* darker green, 4.5:1 against white (safe even for normal text) */
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
}
.card-desc {
  color: #595959;
}
.card-btn {
  background: #007a00;
  color: #ffffff;
  border: none;
  padding: 10px;
}
